NAME
    ps, jobs - list active jobs, breakpoints, watches, and sessions

SYNOPSIS
    ps
    jobs

DESCRIPTION
    Displays a combined table of active items reported by loaded modules
    and the session manager:

    bp<N>       Active breakpoints (emusen.trace).
    watch<N>    Active watches (emusen.trace).
    chd<N>      Running CHD conversion jobs (emusen.library).
    pkg<N>      Running package jobs (emusen.library).
    rom<N>      Running ROM jobs (emusen.library).
    cores<N>    Running core install/update jobs (emusen.cores).
    scrape<N>   Running metadata scrape jobs (emusen.scrape).
    <session>   Named tmux(1) sessions (when enabled by the host).

    'jobs' is a built-in alias for ps. Every listed id can be passed
    directly to kill(1). When nothing is active, ps prints a message
    stating there are no active breakpoints, watches, or sessions.

EXAMPLES
    ps
    jobs

EXIT STATUS
    0   Always succeeds unless a module job query faults.

SEE ALSO
    kill(1), tmux(1), bp(1), watch(1)
